# Bash Programming Practical



## Practical 1: Hello World Program

### Objective

Learn how to create and execute the first Bash script.

### Theory

A Bash script is a text file containing Linux commands that are executed sequentially. The first line of every Bash script usually contains the interpreter path.

### Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Hello Students"
echo "Welcome to Bash Programming"
```

### Explanation

| Statement   | Description                |
| ----------- | -------------------------- |
| #!/bin/bash | Specifies Bash interpreter |
| echo        | Displays text on terminal  |

### Execution

```bash
chmod +x hello.sh
./hello.sh
```

### Output

```text
Hello Students
Welcome to Bash Programming
```




# Practical 2: Variables

## Objective

Understand variable declaration and usage.

### Theory

Variables store information that can be reused throughout the script.

### Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

name="Shivraj"
course="Cybersecurity"

echo "Student Name: $name"
echo "Course: $course"
```

### Explanation

| Statement      | Description              |
| -------------- | ------------------------ |
| name="Shivraj" | Creates variable         |
| $name          | Retrieves variable value |

### Output

```text
Student Name: Shivraj
Course: Cybersecurity
```





# Practical 3: User Input

## Objective

Accept input from users.

### Theory

The read command accepts input from the keyboard and stores it in a variable.

### Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Enter Your Name:"
read name

echo "Welcome $name"
```

### Execution

```bash
chmod +x input.sh
./input.sh
```

### Output

```text
Enter Your Name:
Rahul

Welcome Rahul
```




# Practical 4: Simple Calculator

## Objective

Perform arithmetic operations.

### Theory

Bash supports arithmetic using the (( )) operator.

### Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Enter First Number:"
read a

echo "Enter Second Number:"
read b

echo "Addition = $((a+b))"
echo "Subtraction = $((a-b))"
echo "Multiplication = $((a*b))"
echo "Division = $((a/b))"
```

### Sample Output

```text
Enter First Number:
20

Enter Second Number:
10

Addition = 30
Subtraction = 10
Multiplication = 200
Division = 2
```



